   "id": "sighted",
   "title": "Two fleets in the gulf approaches",
   "time": "Dawn, 7 October",
   "narrative": "After weeks of quarrels and a stormy crossing from Messina, the Holy League fleet left its anchorage on Kefalonia before dawn and rowed east toward the Gulf of Patras. The Ottoman fleet, which had left Lepanto to meet it, came out of the gulf from the opposite side. Both commanders held councils. Doria and others urged caution, but John of Austria wanted a battle to keep the alliance together. Ali Pasha, against the advice of Mehmed Sirocco, chose to fight on his sultan's orders. Positions at sea are reconstructed.",
