   "id": "league-forms",
   "title": "The Holy League forms its line",
   "time": "Morning",
   "narrative": "The League sailed already arranged in four divisions, with galleys of every nation mixed together and Spanish and Italian infantry in each, a lesson drawn from the failure at Preveza in 1538. The Left, of 53 galleys mostly Venetian, lay in the north under Agostino Barbarigo. John of Austria held the Centre with 62 galleys, and Giovanni Andrea Doria commanded the Right of 53 to the south. Alvaro de Bazan's 38 galleys followed as a reserve. A contrary wind slowed the deployment, but around noon it shifted in the Christians' favour.",
