   "title": "The Ottoman crescent",
   "time": "Around 11:00",
   "narrative": "The Ottomans came on in a broad crescent. Mehmed Sirocco commanded 54 galleys on the right, hugging the northern shore. Ali Pasha led 88 galleys and eight galliots in the centre aboard the Sultana. Uluc Ali, with 61 galleys and 32 galliots, took the left to the south and out to sea. A small reserve of eight galleys and 21 galliots stayed behind the centre. The Ottomans had many more soldiers aboard but fewer of the elite janissaries, and their rowers were nearly all slaves.",
